WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.543
CVA6 breaks simplistic decoding.

2
00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:11.603
Its repository name indicates CORE-V, application direction, and six stages; CV64A60 is the formal naming example.

3
00:00:11.603 --> 00:00:21.139
The user guide lists configurations with different width, privilege, ISA, and targets, and still calls CV32A60X interim.

4
00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:29.643
Newer evidence matters: Releases now includes CV32A60X 6.0.0, while the documentation index links CV32A65X.

5
00:00:29.643 --> 00:00:33.775
Read the name together with source date and release.

